  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/zipball/v3.30.0",
  "body": "> [!NOTE]\r\n> ### Datadog tracer bumped to 2.40\r\n> This release bumps the `dd-trace-rb` dependency floor to `2.40` and adds support for the `ap-east-2` and `ap-southeast-6` AWS regions.\r\n\r\n```yml\r\n# AWS Commercial\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-2:30\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-2-ARM:30\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-3:30\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-3-ARM:30\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-4:30\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-4-ARM:30\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Ruby4-0:30\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Ruby4-0-ARM:30\r\n\r\n# AWS GovCloud\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-2:30\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-2-ARM:30\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-3:30\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-3-ARM:30\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-4:30\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Ruby3-4-ARM:30\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Ruby4-0:30\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Ruby4-0-ARM:30\r\n\r\nACCOUNT =\r\n002406178527 for us1 environment\r\n486696501492 for us2 environment\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n- **Bump `dd-trace-rb` dependency floor to `2.40`** — brings the latest tracer improvements and fixes to Ruby Lambda functions. (#164)\r\n- **New AWS regions** — adds `ap-east-2` and `ap-southeast-6` to the supported publish matrix. (#161)\r\n- **AppSec SLS gap coverage** — [APPSEC-68196] closes gaps for AppSec products in serverless. (#162)\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n* update snapshots by @ojproductions in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/pull/159\r\n* Move publish rubygems to Github Actions trusted publisher workflow by @rithikanarayan in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/pull/157\r\n* Add ap-east-2 and ap-southeast-6 to supported regions by @jcstorms1 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/pull/161\r\n* Fix async-metrics integration-test flake (blank log line) by @Strech in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/pull/163\r\n* [APPSEC-68196] Cover gaps for AppSec products in SLS by @Strech in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/pull/162\r\n* Bump datadog dependency floor to 2.40 by @Strech in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/pull/164\r\n* bump minor version to 3.30.0 by @lucaspimentel in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/pull/165\r\n\r\n## New Contributors\r\n* @lucaspimentel made their first contribution in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/pull/165\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-rb/compare/v3.29.0...v3.30.0",
